#!/bin/sh
cat <<'MSG'

mali-vendor-krane installed. Two things are still needed:

  1. The driver itself. It is under ARM's EULA and cannot be shipped, and the
     only Mali-G72 build for Linux is ChromeOS's. Mount a ChromeOS recovery
     image and run:

         mali-vendor-setup /path/to/ROOT-A

  2. A kernel with the Mali kbase driver and a "system" dma-heap, and the GPU
     device tree node kbase expects. See
     /usr/share/doc/mali-vendor-krane/README.md.

Panfrost and kbase claim the same device tree node, so only one of them can be
bound at a time.

MSG
exit 0
